  "Question": "How many digits are in the product \\(4^5 \\cdot 5^{10}?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(8\\)",
    "B": "\\(9\\)",
    "C": "\\(10\\)",
    "D": "\\(11\\)",
    "E": "\\(15\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "A factor of \\(2\\) paired with a factor of \\(5\\) makes \\(10\\), so rewrite \\(4\\) as \\(2^2\\). Then\n\\[\n4^5\\cdot5^{10}\n=(2^2)^5\\cdot5^{10}\n=2^{10}\\cdot5^{10}\n=10^{10}.\n\\]\nThere are ten factors of \\(2\\) and ten factors of \\(5\\), giving ten factors of \\(10\\). Thus the product is \\(1\\) followed by ten zeros, which has \\(11\\) digits. The answer is choice D.",
